From b01f14d7cfb45596d33818a2b5cce7e1150b1e6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:20:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] The capability decision log has one writer, and three
 checks see what they claim
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Found by a sweep of the repository's checks against what CLAUDE.md says they
enforce.

0025 revokes erp_app's INSERT on erp.capability_decision and drops the
policy that admitted any row. 0010 granted both and then routed every
decision through erp.decide_capability(), which writes as its owner, so the
grant stood unused. erp_edge is erp_app, so the edge credential could
append a decision directly, skipping what that function checks: an actor
who may administer capabilities (CAP-P03), CAP-P07 and CAP-P08, and the
state that follows (CAP-P04). The log refuses correction, so a row like
that would stand for good. 0011 had made exactly this rule for its own log
and named 0010 as the exception. Nothing that writes the log changes: the
function, the seeds and the switch-ons all insert as the owner, which the
dropped policy never named. Staging has 0010 but no login role inheriting
erp_app, since 0014 is not applied there; its next rebuild takes 0025.

db-check:
- every-decision-log-is-append-only now refuses an INSERT grant to erp_app
  on any log but the event log, which the branch runtime appends to by
  design, and to erp_read on any log. It reported the capability log until
  0025.
- no-erp-object-in-public covers sequences, foreign tables, composite types,
  routines and types, not only tables and views. A routine created without
  its schema lands in public, and PostgREST serves it to the anon key.
  Extension members are left to no-extension-in-public. Read-only on
  staging, public holds nothing of the kind, and postgres bypasses RLS.
- every-runtime-definer-route-is-gated takes comments and quoted strings out
  of a route's source first, in one pass that reads them in order, so a
  mention in a comment or a string no longer counts as a call.
- The runner reads each assertion through a wrapper, so a violation whose
  text is NULL or blank counts. psql printed it as an empty line, which was
  dropped, so cashier-actors-resolve-to-a-person's actor_id-is-null half
  could never fail.

Controls, run on every db:check:
- three blank violations read as three;
- a routine, a sequence and a domain left in public are reported;
- a route that only mentions the gate, in a line comment, a block comment
  and a string, is reported, and one that calls it after a comment with an
  apostrophe and a string holding "--" is not.

Each fix was reverted in a copy of the tree, and db:check failed with
exactly the matching check:
- 0025 removed;
- the old public query;
- the old strpos;
- the old runner;
- comments stripped before strings, which reported the gated route.

pgTAP:
- 060 asserts the runtime holds no INSERT on the log;
- 010 mirrors the wider public check.
Both fail on the scratch database with the grant restored or a function
left in public.

Docs: CLAUDE.md's four rows, ADR-0022's addendum, and the consolidation
plan's note on 0010.

These pass:
- npm run db:check (133);
- db:fixtures;
- every pgTAP suite but 040, which needs Supabase's storage schema;
- verify (695 tests);
- secret:scan;
- dep:policy.

Requirements: CAP-P03 · CAP-P04 · CAP-P07 · CAP-P08 · SEC-006

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
